        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Per ITU-T X.509 and IETF RFC 5280 (as updated by updated by IETF RFC 6818, IETF RFC 8398 and IETF RFC 8399), some fields/parameters/attributes/data types (or sub-fields/sub-parameters/sub-attributes/sub-data types or sub-sub-fields/sub-sub-parameters/sub-sub-attributes/sub-sub-data types or etc.) can take a sequence of sub-fields/sub-parameters/sub-attributes/sub-data types (or a sequence of sub-sub-fields/sub-sub-parameters/sub-sub-attributes/sub-sub-data types or etc.). Certificate profiles defined by this annex limit the number of sequences of sub-fields/sub-parameters/sub-attributes/sub-data types (or sub-sub-fields/sub-sub-parameters/sub-sub-attributes/sub-sub-data types or etc.) to as defined by this document.",
